          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateReport"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATEREPORT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775476635832",
          "id": "1775457700999",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775457701000_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given one or more inputs. Use only the data present in the inputs. Do not infer, invent, or fill in any missing information.\n\nInput A: {{$context.$nodes.READHIGHVALUEORDERSDATA.$output}}\nInput B: {{$context.$nodes.FETCHBATCHDETAILS.$output}}\nInput C: {{$context.$nodes.FORMATDATA.$output.result}}\n\nYour task is to generate a report with properly formatted multiRecordWidgets suitable for PDF generation.\n\n======================================================================\nTASK 1: High Value Orders – Pick Release Status\n======================================================================\nUse Input A only if it is present and contains a JSON array. Each element contains a field called \"text\", and that field is a JSON string.\n\nFor each valid \"text\" value:\n- Parse the JSON string inside \"text\".\n- Use only records that parse successfully.\n- Skip invalid JSON records.\n- Skip records missing required fields.\n\nCreate exactly TWO multiRecordWidget :\n\n1. Released to Warehouse\n- Include rows where Status = \"S\"\n- Columns: Order, Batch\n- Field mapping: Order = Order, Batch = Batch\n\n2. Backordered\n- Include rows where ReservationStatus = \"U\"\n- Columns: Order, Batch\n- Field mapping: Order = Order, Batch = Batch\n\nRules:\n- Render each multiRecordWidget \n- Keep each row separate.\n- Do not aggregate or summarize rows.\n- Preserve the original input order.\n- If no valid rows exist for a section, do not show that section.\n\n======================================================================\nTASK 2: Batch Processing Report\n======================================================================\nUse Input B and Input C if both are present. Input C.result contains an array of batch objects.\n\nFor each batch object in Input C.result:\n1. Create a separate multiRecordWidget titled: Batch: <BatchId>\n2. Find rows in Input B whose Order matches any Order in that batch's priorityOrders array.\n3. Include only matching rows for that batch.\n4. Display the matching rows in a multiRecordWidget with columns:\n   - Order\n   - Customer\n   - Item\n   - Requested Quantity\n   - UOM\n   - Status\n   - Amount\n\nField mapping:\n- Order = Order\n- Customer = SoldToCustomer\n- Item = Item\n- Requested Quantity = RequestedQuantity\n- UOM = RequestedQuantityUOM\n- Status = LineStatus\n- Amount = LineUnitPrice * RequestedQuantity\n\nRules:\n- Use only matching rows from Input B.\n- Do not infer missing values.\n- Do not add rows that do not match.\n- Preserve input order where possible.\n- Render each batch's data as a proper multiRecord widget .\n- Show one heading per batch.\n- Under each batch heading, show only the matching multiRecordWidget rows.\n- If a batch has no matching rows, do not show the batch.\n\nIMPORTANT: Ensure that the data from Input B is correctly matched and included for each batch from Input C.result.\nIf no matching rows are found for a batch, omit that batch from the report.\n\n======================================================================\nOUTPUT RULES\n======================================================================\n- If Task 1 applies, show the \"High Value Orders – Pick Release Status\" section first.\n- If Task 2 applies, show the \"Batch Processing Report\" section after that.\n- Use clean report formatting with proper widget .\n- Do not include explanations, JSON, or extra commentary.\n- Do not add any text outside the required headings, descriptions, and multiRecordWidgets."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
