          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Reservation Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_RESERVATION_DATA",
          "id": "1776333529068",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776333529069_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.READVECTOREFORFUTURERSV.$output}}\n\nThe above input is a JSON array where each element contains a field \"text\" which itself is a JSON string. Parse the JSON inside each \"text\" field and use only that data.\n\nDisplay a heading and a one-line description before the tables:\n- Heading: \"Reservation Summary\"\n- Description: \"Overview of reserved and unreserved order lines.\"\n\nCreate exactly TWO tables:\n1. Reserved (ReservationStatus = \"R\")\n2. Not Reserved (ReservationStatus = \"U\")\n\nEach table must have the following columns:\n- Order\n- Item\n- Reservation Quantity\n- UOM\n- Status\n\nField mapping:\n- Order = Order\n- Item = Item\n- Reservation Quantity = RequestedQuantity\n- UOM = RequestedQuantityUOM\n- Status = \"Reserved\" if ReservationStatus = \"R\", \"Not Reserved\" if ReservationStatus = \"U\"\n\nRules:\n- Use only data from the parsed \"text\" JSON.\n- Do not infer or add missing values.\n- Skip records with invalid JSON in \"text\".\n- Skip records missing required fields.\n- Do not aggregate; each record should be one row.\n- Preserve input order.\n\nEdge cases:\n- If no records exist, show both tables with:\n  - \"No reserved records found.\"\n  - \"No records found without reservation.\"\n- If only one type exists, show only the table having data\n\nOutput format:\n- First show the heading and description\n- Then Reserved table\n- Then Unreserved table\n\n- Do not include any extra explanation beyond the single description line"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
