          "code": "FILTERPRIORITYANDHIGHVALUEORDERS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776767417286",
          "id": "1775214432117",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775214432118_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given an input array of order line records: {{$context.$nodes.GETFUTUREORDERS.$output.items}}.\n\nAdditional inputs:\n- High value threshold: {{$context.$variables.OrderHighValueLimit}}\n- Priority code definitions: {{$context.$variables.PriorityCodesDetails}}\n\nEach order may have multiple lines, and the input is already sorted by Order number.\n\nFor each Order:\n1. Calculate each line value as:\n   Line Value = LineUnitPrice × RequestedQuantity\n2. Calculate the total Order Value by summing all line values for that Order.\n3. Check whether the Order matches the single priority code defined in {{$context.$variables.PriorityCodesDetails}}.\n\nReturn the result in this exact JSON format:\n\n{\n  \"priorityOrders\": [\n    {\n      \"Order\": \"\",\n      \"TotalOrderValue\": 0,\n      \"ShippingPriorityCode\": \"\",\n      \"IsHighValue\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"highValueOrders\": [\n    {\n      \"Order\": \"\",\n      \"TotalOrderValue\": 0,\n      \"ShippingPriorityCode\": \"\",\n      \"SourceSystem\":\"\",\n      \"OrderTypeCode\":\"\",\n      \"IsHighValue\": true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- `priorityOrders` must contain only orders matching the priority code.\n- `highValueOrders` must contain only orders whose total order value is greater than or equal to {{$context.$variables.OrderHighValueLimit}}.\n- Do not include any extra text, explanation, or markdown.\n- Each order should appear only once in each list."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
